  "consentTitle": "Turn on maps",
  "consentHeading": "This is the only\npart that uses\nthe internet",
  "consentIntro": "Everything else in Quiet Places stays on your phone. Your Quiet Places, their names, your history — none of it is ever sent anywhere, with or without maps.",
  "consentSentTitle": "WHAT GETS SENT",
  "consentSentBody": "Requests to OpenStreetMap for the map squares on your screen. Each request is a map square number, not your coordinates — but at street zoom a square is about 600 m across, so the squares you load do reveal roughly where the place you are editing is. We would rather say that than let you find out later.",
  "consentSearchTitle": "SEARCH AND PLACE NAMES",
  "consentSearchBody": "If you search for an address, that text is sent to OpenStreetMap's search service. When you finish moving the pin, its coordinates are sent once to look up a name to suggest — only when you let go, never continuously, and the answer is reused if you nudge it again. You can always type the name yourself instead.",
  "consentNeverTitle": "WHAT NEVER GETS SENT",
  "consentNeverBody": "Your saved places, their names, your entry and exit history, your settings. There is no analytics, no crash reporting, and no account.",
  "consentWhoTitle": "WHO RECEIVES IT",
  "consentWhoBody": "The OpenStreetMap Foundation's tile and search servers. They see the request and your IP address, as any website would. We send a User-Agent naming this app, which their usage policy requires, and we rate-limit what we send.",
  "consentOffTitle": "YOU CAN TURN IT BACK OFF",
  "consentOffBody": "Maps can be switched off again in Settings at any time, and the map cache cleared. With maps off the app makes no network requests at all.",
  "consentFallback": "Without maps, the editor still works: you place a Quiet Place from where you are standing, or by typing coordinates, and set the radius on the dial.",
  "consentAccept": "TURN ON MAPS",
  "consentDecline": "KEEP THE APP OFFLINE",
