  "permBackgroundTitle": "Location — \"Allow all the time\"",
  "permBackgroundBody": "Quiet Places only fire in the background with all-the-time access. Denying this means silencing works only while the app is open.",
  "permDndTitle": "Do Not Disturb access",
  "permDndBody": "Required to switch silent/DND modes. This one can't be a normal popup — you grant it on a dedicated system screen.",
  "permDndAction": "Open DND settings",
  "permNotificationsTitle": "Notifications",
  "permNotificationsBodyIos": "iOS can't silence your ringer automatically. Instead we'll notify you on arrival so you can do it (or trigger a Shortcuts Focus automation).",
  "permNotificationsBodyAndroid": "For the brief foreground notice while changing your ringer.",
  "permBatteryTitle": "Ignore battery optimisation",
  "permBatteryBody": "Aggressive battery savers can kill background delivery. Exempting Quiet Places keeps it reliable.",
  "noteOemTitle": "ON XIAOMI / OPPO / VIVO / SAMSUNG",
  "noteOemBody": "These brands add their own \"autostart\" or \"protected apps\" controls that stop background apps. Find Quiet Places in your phone's Battery or App-management settings and enable Autostart / Allow background activity, or Quiet Places may stop firing.",
  "noteIosTitle": "IOS CANNOT SILENCE AUTOMATICALLY",
  "noteIosBody": "Apple provides no API to change the ringer. For a hands-free setup, open Shortcuts → Automation → Create a Location automation for the same place and set it to turn on a Focus mode. Quiet Places still notifies you on arrival as a backup.",
